SillyTavern has been installed in %%WWWDIR%%.

Quick start
===========

Enable the service at boot and start it now:

    sysrc sillytavern_enable=YES
    service sillytavern start

Then open:

    http://127.0.0.1:8000/

The first start copies the bundled default content (characters, themes,
presets) into the data directory and can take a few seconds.

Configuration and data
======================

The main configuration file is %%ETCDIR%%/config.yaml. It is created from
config.yaml.sample during installation and is left untouched by package
upgrades. It controls the port, listen address, IP whitelist, SSL,
authentication and other server options.

Characters, chats, presets, uploads and backups are stored separately in
/var/db/sillytavern, so upgrading or reinstalling the port does not remove
user data.

Logs
====

    /var/log/sillytavern.log            service output
    /var/db/sillytavern/access.log      HTTP access log

Network access
==============

The default configuration listens on 127.0.0.1 only. To let other machines
connect, set "listen: true" in %%ETCDIR%%/config.yaml and add their
addresses or subnets to "whitelist" (by default only 127.0.0.1 and ::1 are
allowed), then restart the service.

For remote access without opening the port, use an SSH tunnel:

    ssh -L 8000:127.0.0.1:8000 user@this-host

Service management
==================

    service sillytavern start|stop|restart|status
    tail -f /var/log/sillytavern.log

Additional command line options can be passed through sillytavern_flags in
/etc/rc.conf.

Updating
========

The application files in %%WWWDIR%% are managed by pkg. Rebuild the port or
use pkg upgrade to update them; %%ETCDIR%%/config.yaml and
/var/db/sillytavern are preserved.
